 attacking Thor  Korg and King Valkyrie are there to  fight them off during the battle Thor  Hears A Familiar sound looking around  the chaos of battle he sees his  reconstructed mjolnir just as the hammer  is about to reach his hand it flies back  to its current Master Jane Foster things  turn into a violent and epic romantic  comedy as the two banter a bit before  Gore goes on the attack then we learn  this is all a ruse for Gore to capture  the children and hide them in the shadow  realm the seamless tonal shifts are very  impressive and the moment Jane holds me  only here is a stand-up and clap moment  with Thanos Marvel created someone who  is multi-dimensional with a point of  view you could understand even though  you probably don't agree with him  they've done this again in Thor love and  thunder in the form of Gore the god  butcher from his first appearance you  understand why he's so angry and  vengeful he was clearly a devoted  disciple of a God who betrayed him with  indifference that would be enough for us  to understand him but we empathize  because he's so complicated on a visual  level he looks haunted and creepy  however Christian Bale's voice isn't  Heavy Deep raspy in a few scenes his  voice is high pitched almost wounded for  instance take the scene in which he  emerges from the Shadows intentionally  terrifying the children he's captured by  producing a creature and ripping its  head off in a horrifying display of  dominance he doesn't smile he doesn't  laugh instead he looks sad tired and  confused it's worth watching again for  the shock of how dark the moment is and  to savor the nuances of the performance  since Gore exists in the shadow realm  Thor and Friends need to borrow Zeus's  weapon Thunderbolt to fight the darkness  this brings them to the incredible  omnipotent City where all the gods  reside everything about this place  deserves a re-watch because it is so  beautiful and packed with Easter eggs  and references at only multiple vie