int of the scene the reason  this moment is so powerful is witnessing  just how brutal Gore can be he moves  through the Shadows like a reanimated  corpse he speaks through sharp rotten  teeth and even tortures Thor to make him  call his ax some viewers may not wish to  relive such an aggressively dark scene  but the strength of the performances  should be enough to bring it back  there was a time when the primary  audience for superhero stories was kids  adult fans may not like to admit this  fact but it's true as new creators  entered the comic book industry they  started updating their stories to  reflect their interests and eventually  superhero comics matured to a point  where most parents probably wouldn't  allow their kids to read them until  reaching some mutually agreed upon age  we have lived in this Paradigm for so  long that it's easy to forget the more  innocent origins of our favorite  characters family and kid-friendly  Comics still exist of course but the  vast majority of superhero films are  aimed at older audiences as why it is so  rewarding when Thor shares his powers  with the kidnapped children for the  first time in an MCU movie we see kids  take on the bad guys and it is pure  thrilling wish fulfillment as the song  November Rain kicks into gear the kids  Strike Back lightning erupts from their  eyes and weapons as they defeat their  captors and Thor does battle with Gore  for anyone who fell in love with  superheroes at a young age this is a  dream come true  like the opening the ending of Thor love  and thunder is surprisingly lacking in  the epic battle sequence Department  Marvel films have a habit of ending with  two super powered beans punching each  other into exhaustion and the one left  standing is the Victor but love and  thunder begins its climax that way  before careening into Uncharted  Territory for the MCU 4 reaches eternity  Jane is succumbing to her illness and  Thor doesn't know quite what to do  losing the love of his life 